{"parentUuid": null, "isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "C:/puck/.claude/worktrees/lod-hysteresis", "sessionId": "722129d2-be07-5b7d-bcee-11d4c960fa60", "version": "2.1.316", "gitBranch": "worktree-lod-hysteresis", "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "Brief `lod-hysteresis` (implementer, claude-sonnet-5-5: a contained C# change with a focused test).\n\nTask: give LOD selection hysteresis, so a prop standing on a band boundary stops flipping between levels every frame. `LodSelector.Select` in `src/Puck.World.Presentation/Lod/LodSelector.cs` picks the level from distance alone; keep the previous level until the distance passes the boundary by `LodBand.Hysteresis`, which `LodBand.cs` already declares and nothing reads.\n\nIntegration branch: `lead/fundamentals`. You may write `src/Puck.World.Presentation/Lod/` and `worlds/debug/lod-tests.puck`.\n\nFinish line: `Puck.World.Presentation` builds, and `puck test worlds/debug/lod-tests.puck --jobs 1` passes on the merged head under the heavy lease.\n\nStopping condition: a look call (how wide the band should feel). No GPU leg."}, "uuid": "73a150b5-26e2-54d4-bc8e-40524ea14da1", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T14:02:15.000Z"}
